; Call a handler address if it is not zero
;
; Calls the routine at HL (through #R$9B80) when HL is not zero, and does
; nothing when it is. All registers except AF are preserved, so the handler can
; not hand values back in registers. Used for the handler words in records,
; timers and NPC scripts.
; .
; HL Address of the handler, or 0 for none
@label=CallHandler
c$9B6C PUSH IX       ;
 $9B6E PUSH IY       ;
 $9B70 PUSH DE       ;
 $9B71 PUSH BC       ;
 $9B72 PUSH HL       ;
 $9B73 LD A,L        ;
 $9B74 OR H          ;
 $9B75 CALL NZ,$9B80 ; JP (HL) trampoline
 $9B78 POP HL        ;
 $9B79 POP BC        ;
 $9B7A POP DE        ;
 $9B7B POP IY        ;
 $9B7D POP IX        ;
 $9B7F RET           ;
